---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import { Grid, Card, Badge } from "webcoreui/astro";
import DeckSection from "@components/DeckSection.astro";
import DecklistTooltip from "@components/DecklistTooltip.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Lists - Replenish Guide"
    prev={{ name: "Sideboard", href: "/sideboard" }}
    next={{ name: "Mechanics", href: "/mechanics" }}
>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 3rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Lists
    </h1>
    <p
        style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-20); max-width: 650px; line-height: 1.6;"
    >
        Below are four different configurations of Parallax Replenish, ranging
        from stock modern builds to classic lists and experimental control
        variants.
    </p>

    <h2>Key Differences</h2>
    <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <strong>Decree of Silence (3 vs. 2):</strong> Three is relevant in situations
            where Replenish is likely to resolve and Opal+Wave does not necessarily
            mean an immediate win. Matchups like Sligh, the mirror, Enchantress, BW
            Control, and decks with Tranquil Domain fall into this category. You go
            down to two when the opposite is true: when Replenish is hard to resolve,
            or when resolving an Opal+Wave is enough to win the game by itself. In
            those situations, having fewer Decrees clogging up your hand is much better
            (especially since against control you side out discard outlets like Frantic
            Search anyway).
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <strong>Seal of Cleansing (4 vs. 3 in the 75):</strong> Running four total
            is a luxury. It's gotten better with the rise of Aluren, the Replenish
            mirror, Enchantress, and other enchantment-heavy decks. Three in the 75
            is the leaner option if those matchups are less common in your field.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <strong>Tsabo’s Web (3 vs. 2):</strong> Some lists run three because their
            local region has a lot of Terrageddon and Port. Online, Terrageddon has
            been trending down, so the count is closer to two in the 75 for most general
            builds.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <strong>Maindeck vs Sideboard Creatures:</strong> Bryan Gulotta's list
            puts 4 Meddling Mages in the maindeck for proactive protection against
            fast combo and control, while lists like Alessandro's keep them in the
            sideboard to blank opposing removal Game 1.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div
        style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;"
    >
        {/* List 1: Alessandro Galli */}
        <Card>
            <h2 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.5rem;">Alessandro Galli</h2>
            <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <Badge theme="info" small={true}
                    >4Seasons Spring Ed. @ Bologna (2026)</Badge
                >
            </div>

            <Grid column={3} gap="lg">
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Combo / Engine"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Replenish" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Attunement" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Opalescence" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Parallax Wave" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Decree of Silence" },
                        ]}
                    />

                    <DeckSection
                        title="Card Selection"
                        items={[
                            { count: 3, name: "Frantic Search" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Intuition" },
                        ]}
                    />
                </div>
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Interaction / Protection"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Swords to Plowshares" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Seal of Cleansing" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Abeyance" },
                        ]}
                    />

                    <DeckSection
                        title="Lands (25)"
                        items={[
                            { count: 5, name: "Island" },
                            { count: 5, name: "Plains" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Adarkar Wastes" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Ancient Tomb" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Flooded Strand" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Skycloud Expanse" },
                        ]}
                    />
                </div>
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Sideboard (15)"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Meddling Mage" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Defense Grid" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Hydroblast" },
                            { count: 2, name: "Exalted Angel" },
                            { count: 2, name: "Tsabo's Web" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Seal of Cleansing" },
                        ]}
                    />
                </div>
            </Grid>
        </Card>

        {/* List 2: Brian Siu */}
